- action: CREATE
  id: project-setup
  title: Python project structure, dependencies, and configuration setup
  acceptance_criteria:
    - Initialize Python project with proper directory structure
    - Create requirements.txt with all dependencies (playwright, openai, pyyaml, pillow)
    - Create config.yaml configuration file with start URL, LLM provider settings, browser settings, exploration limits, and output directory settings
    - Set up output directory structure (events, screenshots)
    - Basic project README with setup instructions
  dependencies: []

- action: CREATE
  id: browser-controller
  title: Playwright-based browser controller for page navigation
  acceptance_criteria:
    - Implement BrowserController class that initializes Playwright browser in headless mode
    - Provides page loading with proper wait conditions
    - Implements navigation methods (goto, back, reload)
    - Handles browser lifecycle (startup, shutdown)
    - Includes error handling and retry logic for network issues
    - Waits for network idle before considering page loaded
    - Unit tests for basic navigation scenarios
  dependencies:
    - project-setup

- action: CREATE
  id: event-capture
  title: Network request interception to capture analytics events
  acceptance_criteria:
    - Implement EventCapture class that sets up Playwright network request interception
    - Filters requests matching pattern _analytics/publish_event?type=EVENT_TYPE
    - Extracts event type from URL parameters
    - Parses request body to extract event metadata (event field)
    - Returns structured event data with timestamp
    - Handles malformed requests gracefully
    - Unit tests with mock network requests
  dependencies:
    - project-setup
    - browser-controller

- action: CREATE
  id: element-identifier
  title: DOM analysis to identify interactive elements on pages
  acceptance_criteria:
    - Implement ElementIdentifier class that extracts all interactive elements (buttons, links, inputs, selects, clickable divs)
    - Generates descriptions for each element (text content, aria-label, role, tag name)
    - Captures element bounding boxes and coordinates
    - Filters out hidden, disabled, or duplicate elements
    - Returns list of interactive elements with metadata
    - Handles dynamic DOM changes
    - Unit tests with mock DOM structures
  dependencies:
    - project-setup
    - browser-controller

- action: CREATE
  id: screenshot-capture
  title: Screenshot capture functionality integrated with browser controller
  acceptance_criteria:
    - Extend BrowserController or create ScreenshotCapture class that captures full-page screenshots
    - Generates filenames with timestamp and URL slug
    - Saves screenshots to configured directory
    - Optionally highlights specific elements on screenshots
    - Returns path to saved screenshot
    - Handle viewport scrolling for full-page captures
    - Unit tests for screenshot generation
  dependencies:
    - project-setup
    - browser-controller

- action: CREATE
  id: data-collector
  title: JSON data storage and file organization
  acceptance_criteria:
    - Implement DataCollector class that accepts event data with all required fields (event type, metadata, URLs, element description, screenshot path, element location, timestamp)
    - Writes events to JSONL file (one event per line)
    - Creates organized directory structure
    - Handles file I/O errors gracefully
    - Provides method to flush data to disk
    - Define clear data schema matching the plan
    - Unit tests for data writing and schema validation
  dependencies:
    - project-setup

- action: CREATE
  id: llm-navigator
  title: OpenAI LLM integration for intelligent navigation
  acceptance_criteria:
    - Implement LLMNavigator class that integrates with OpenAI API
    - Creates prompt templates for element selection
    - Sends page context plus element list to LLM
    - Parses LLM response to select next element to interact with
    - Determines if interaction will trigger navigation
    - Decides when to explore new pages vs continue on current page
    - Handles LLM API errors and rate limits (exponential backoff)
    - Respects depth limits to prevent infinite exploration
    - Configuration for LLM parameters (model, temperature, API key)
    - Unit tests with mocked LLM responses
  dependencies:
    - project-setup

- action: CREATE
  id: navigation-stack
  title: Stack management for page exploration state
  acceptance_criteria:
    - Implement NavigationStack class that maintains stack/queue of pages to explore
    - Tracks navigation history (previous page URLs)
    - Records which elements have been interacted with per page
    - Prevents duplicate exploration of same page+element combinations
    - Provides methods to push/pop pages
    - Tracks current depth in navigation tree
    - Enforces max depth and max pages limits
    - Unit tests for stack operations and deduplication
  dependencies:
    - project-setup

- action: CREATE
  id: element-interaction
  title: Safe element interaction handling
  acceptance_criteria:
    - Implement element interaction logic that safely interacts with different element types (click, type, select)
    - Validates elements exist and are visible before interaction
    - Waits for potential navigation after interaction
    - Captures events that occur before navigation
    - Handles popups, modals, and alerts
    - Implements proper waiting and retry logic
    - Handles interaction failures gracefully
    - Integration with BrowserController and EventCapture
    - Unit tests for various interaction scenarios
  dependencies:
    - project-setup
    - browser-controller
    - element-identifier

- action: CREATE
  id: main-orchestration
  title: Main entry point that orchestrates all components
  acceptance_criteria:
    - Implement main script that loads configuration from YAML file
    - Initializes all components (browser, event capture, LLM, etc.)
    - Implements main exploration loop (pop page, load, screenshot, identify elements, LLM selection, interact, capture events, push new pages)
    - Sets up logging and progress reporting
    - Handles graceful shutdown on interruption (Ctrl+C)
    - Comprehensive error handling throughout
    - Command-line interface for running the script
    - Integration tests with all components
  dependencies:
    - project-setup
    - browser-controller
    - event-capture
    - element-identifier
    - screenshot-capture
    - data-collector
    - llm-navigator
    - navigation-stack
    - element-interaction
